    docs(super): document final HTTP-only migration behavior
    
    Update both EN and ZH READMEs with completed non-VPP behaviors:
    
    - STUN URIs: both stun:host:port and stun://host:port accepted; hosts may
      be IP literals or syntactically valid DNS hostnames; validation performs
      no DNS I/O; resolution happens at runtime inside SuperSTUNManager.
      Generic endpoint parsing (conn/conn.go) remains IP-literal-only.
    
    - SSE with polling fallback: polling is fallback-only — Sync establishes
      SSE first, starts polling only after stream failure, cancels polling as
      soon as stream is healthy. Hub close terminates SSE streams.
    
    - Edge config legacy rejection: LegacySuper key and DynamicRoute.SuperNode
      key (including UseSuperNode: false) rejected with legacy_udp_field error.
    
    - Super config legacy rejection: all 7 v1 fields rejected by pre-scan
      (PrivKeyV4..ListenPort_ManageAPI). mtypes.SuperConfig/SuperInfo retired.
    
    - VPP excluded: make vpp never validated on libmemif-equipped host.
    
    Contract tests added to docs_contract_test.go verify no stale wording
    reverts (IP literals only, always-on polling, missing legacy fields,
    missing VPP exclusion, missing Edge rejection).
    
